## Contributing

When you want to contribute to a repo, clone the main repo & make a branch (**don’t fork the repo!**).

Categorize your branches under the following sections

{% table %}
- Branch Folder
- Description
---
- features/
- Feature work
---
- tasks/
- Task work
---
- bugs/
- Bug fixes
---
- releases/
- Milestone releases
---
- docs/
- Documentation changes
{% /table %}

Ensure that the branch's name is all lowercase and follows kebab-case

### Merging Contibutions

The team merges contributions using two methods:

**Rebase & merge**: the standard way to merge changes

**Squash & merge**: for overly messy PRs (ex. CI/CD testing)

---

## Deployments

Code deployment is organized into various branches. These conventions depend on the situation and the repo.

{% table %}
- Repo
- Branch Folder
- Description
---
- All
- main or master
- Staging deployments/latest changes
---
- p3d-web, p3d-docs
- prod
- Production deployments
---
- persona-3-dual
- releases/
- Milestone releases
---
- All
- tester/
- Specific tester changes
{% /table %}

---

